body:
@Calinou depth biasing has been in Vulkan since 1.0, so why can't we use that?

It's the direct modern equivalent of `glPolygonOffset`, so maybe I'm a little confused. Can you clarify?

```cpp
VkPipelineRasterizationStateCreateInfo {
    depthBiasEnable = VK_TRUE,
    depthBiasConstantFactor = ...,
    depthBiasClamp = ...,
    depthBiasSlopeFactor = ...
}
```

@Calinou Yes, and apparently the code is already inside the Godot driver initializers for all of them

https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agodotengine%2Fgodot%20depthbias&type=code

I'm just glad it can help, I could use this for a couple of projects. I will add, I would like to see this available in general materials since it allows separation of testing from writing unlike writing `DEPTH` in the fragment shader does and is also more widely supported.
